<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/vipasca"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vipasca.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Vipasca</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Vipasca was a Roman mining settlement in Lusitania, at modern Aljustrel in southern Portugal, where copper and silver were extracted.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/vir-singh-deo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vir-singh-deo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Vir Singh Deo</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Vir Singh Deo, also written Bir Singh Deo, was the Bundela Rajput ruler of Orchha from 1605 to 1627.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/vira-alakeshvara"><span class="enc-name">Vira Alakeshvara</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Vira Alakeshvara was the leading figure of the powerful Alagakkonara family in Sri Lanka in the Gampola period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/vira-someshwara"><span class="enc-name">Vira Someshwara</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Vira Someshvara was king of the Hoysala dynasty from 1235 to 1263, the son of Narasimha II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/viracocha"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/viracocha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Viracocha</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Viracocha was the creator god of the Inca and other Andean peoples, believed to have risen from Lake Titicaca and made the sun, moon, stars and the first humans.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/viracocha-inca"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vi